        "Organic growth is anchored by a 15% annual EBITDA growth assumption, supported by DUOL's proven subscription flywheel, expanding premium tier penetration, and accelerating international monetization. The platform's network effects and low churn among paid subscribers provide high visibility into forward revenue, making this growth rate achievable without requiring new product bets.",
        "Margin expansion is the second pillar. A 75% free cash flow conversion rate reflects the inherent operating leverage of DUOL's asset-light SaaS model \u2014 as subscriber counts scale, incremental content and infrastructure costs grow sub-linearly. We expect disciplined G&A rationalization post-close to contribute further to cash generation, funding both debt service and organic reinvestment.",
        "On exit, we underwrite a 14.0x EV/EBITDA multiple, representing a modest 2.0-turn expansion from entry. The projected exit enterprise value of approximately $5.6B reflects this re-rating combined with compounded EBITDA growth. Multiple expansion is conservative relative to SaaS peers that have re-rated materially on sustained top-line growth; even at entry multiples the returns profile is robust."
